<%# The app had connect affordances everywhere and no way to *get* a wallet,
    which assumes every visitor already holds one. HashPack does creation and
    card funding itself, so all we owe the visitor is the pointer — offered at
    the moment they are asked to connect, never as a gate on browsing.
    `note` tailors the reason; the wallet story itself lives only here. %>
<span class="wallet-help t-caption muted">
  No wallet?
  <%= link_to "Create one free with HashPack", "https://www.hashpack.app/",
        target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>
  <%= "— #{note}" if note.present? %>
</span>
